# GEMVC (not Laravel / Symfony)

Installed: **`gemvc/library` 5.16.0** under `vendor/gemvc/`. Before inventing APIs, open:

1. `vendor/gemvc/library/.cursorrules` — hard Do/Don't (root AI front door)
2. `vendor/gemvc/library/README.md` — architecture + AI reading order
3. `vendor/gemvc/library/docs/ai/` — INDEX → CANONICAL → CORE_REFERENCE when present (`--prefer-source` / git); otherwise https://github.com/gemvc/gemvc `docs/ai/`
4. Source of truth for signatures: `vendor/gemvc/library/src/` (Request, Response, ApiService, Controller, Table, ViewTable)

Composer **dist** (default production) omits `docs/` via `.gitattributes` `export-ignore`. Root `.cursorrules` + `README.md` still ship.

## 4 layers (mandatory for HTTP services)

```
API → Controller → Model → Table / ViewTable
```

Naming: `User.php` / `UserController.php` / `UserModel.php` / `UserTable.php` (views: `UserAccessTable extends ViewTable`).

| Layer | Extends | Job |
|-------|---------|-----|
| `app/api/` | `ApiService` / `ProtectedApiService` | schema, `requireAuth` / `auth()`, `requireInternalService()`, `requireRateLimit*()`, `callController()` |
| `app/controller/` | `Controller` | `createModel()`, `mapPostToObject()`, `createList()` |
| `app/model/` | `*Table` / `*ViewTable` or composition | business rules; reshape flat view rows → JSON; `Response::*` |
| `app/table/` | `Table` or `ViewTable` | columns/`$_type_map`; tables: `defineSchema()`; views: `defineView()` + `viewDependsOn()` |

## Hard rules

- **DO** `definePostSchema` / `defineGetSchema` before using input; fail with `$this->request->returnResponse()`
- **DO** `$this->callController(new XController($this->request))->method()` on all servers (Apache/Nginx/FrankenPHP/OpenSwoole)
- **DO** prefer `gemvc/helper` (`CryptHelper`, `TypeChecker`) and `gemvc/http-client` / library `ServiceCall` for outbound HTTP (family mesh)
- **DO** set JWT `$token->role` (comma-separated names) when minting tokens if you rely on `auth(['admin'])`
- **DO** use `setPrimaryKey('col')` after `parent::__construct()` when the Table/ViewTable has no `id` property (views / alternate PKs)
- **DO** use **`ViewTable`** for SQL views: `defineView()`, flat column props matching aliases, `gemvc db:migrate YourViewTable` or `--all`
- **DO** family-only routes: `requireInternalService()`; sibling callers: `ServiceCall::to(...)->withInternalTrust()`
- **DON'T** invent routes files, Eloquent, manual sanitization, or string-concat SQL
- **DON'T** point a plain `Table` at a view and migrate it — that creates a physical table; use `ViewTable`
- **DON'T** invent Eloquent-style 1:n on views — views are flat; nest in the Model after select
- **DON'T** edit `vendor/gemvc/**` — fix app code or bump Composer versions
- Money: `string` + `$_type_map` `decimal` — never `float`; concurrent: `beginTransaction` + `forUpdate` + BCMath on `$this` (not hydrated rows / not raw PDO) — `docs/guides/model.md#atomic-money-transfers-pessimistic-lock`

## Ecosystem map (`vendor/gemvc/`)

| Package | Role |
|---------|------|
| `library` | HTTP, Bootstrap, ApiService, Controller, Table, ViewTable, JWT, CLI (`db:migrate` / `--all`) |
| `helper` | CryptHelper, TypeChecker, ProjectHelper |
| `http-client` | outbound sync/async HTTP |
